# A ghost shown at the end of the file; the user clicks into the middle
# of line 2. Every key already dismissed a ghost; a click moved the
# cursor without one, so the ghost followed it and painted mid-word
# ("secoGHOSTZnd") — and the next Tab, an indent as far as the user
# knew, inserted it there. Any cursor move now clears it.
write a.txt "first line\nsecond line\n"
open a.txt
key ctrl+end
ghost GHOSTZ
expect screen contains "GHOSTZ"
click 40 3
expect screen lacks "GHOSTZ"
key tab
command file.save
expect file a.txt lacks "GHOSTZ"
